==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{borrowing|en|fr|défaitisme}}, coined in 1915 by Russian writer {{w|Grigory Aleksinsky|Grigorij Aleksinskij}} as a translation of {{cog|ru|пораженчество}}, also coined by him as a derivation of {{m|ru|порази́ть||to strike, defeat}}. Surface analysis: {{suffix|en|defeat|ism}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/dɪˈfiːtɪzəm/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-defeatism.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# [[acceptance|Acceptance]] of defeat [[without]] [[struggle]].
#: ''Objective assessment is good but '''defeatism''' will reduce our potentials even when the prospects for victory have never been nearer.''

